my-id "q-17480" :question/problem "What is the first term of an arithmetic series if the common difference is $d=5,$ and the sum of the first $11$ terms is ${S}_{11}=374?$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the common difference of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=11$, $d=5$, and ${S}_{N}=374$ into the formula above, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}374 & =\\frac{11}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(11-1)(5)) \\\\ 748 & =11(2{a}_{1}+50) \\\\ 68 & =2{a}_{1}+50 \\\\ 18 & =2{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-17480/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f9251ee-4d19-5074-a2a3-07e13149260f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-17480"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76376/selection/d69753b89da2a17ea8dd7d9a2b6cb5ccf489cb1956b4dc4d88b98b238c9b4d21" :answer/id #uuid "c1614607-33a3-5a74-acf8-9b58fa05df53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-77" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76376/selection/4f1ffa38d73b18554a47d8d9cea1139f02bb33ce8900fc955ea927ce75c224e3" :answer/id #uuid "f535f8e3-1dd7-563c-9b80-567e9ceb987f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "62" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76376/selection/07d13be2013e30923af5a143315b52581ff8ba40d0c80a016e8b9a5560d0140e" :answer/id #uuid "6c5127d7-7fda-5258-859b-e3cd33af069d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "71" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76376/selection/929d54af1ce3c37c5e2af424428326ec37432c9399788240c1ce5cf5f7c4add1" :answer/id #uuid "5523afe2-da3b-5b98-82f8-083447193ee8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-68" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76376/selection/8cd557fa143c2616f01a8df1d19e854fea26be776628dc106639661d1b774491" :answer/id #uuid "47ce9e12-ee9f-5de3-bb33-df4d10f1bc23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "65" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76376/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6ccf9c26-3ec6-5184-bfa6-411f920bb63a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76376/selection/8cd557fa143c2616f01a8df1d19e854fea26be776628dc106639661d1b774491" :answer-field/choices ["q-76376/selection/d69753b89da2a17ea8dd7d9a2b6cb5ccf489cb1956b4dc4d88b98b238c9b4d21" "q-76376/selection/4f1ffa38d73b18554a47d8d9cea1139f02bb33ce8900fc955ea927ce75c224e3" "q-76376/selection/07d13be2013e30923af5a143315b52581ff8ba40d0c80a016e8b9a5560d0140e" "q-76376/selection/929d54af1ce3c37c5e2af424428326ec37432c9399788240c1ce5cf5f7c4add1" "q-76376/selection/8cd557fa143c2616f01a8df1d19e854fea26be776628dc106639661d1b774491"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76376" :question/id #uuid "07fef979-0133-5e51-8e0b-bfcd37c2daee" :question/math-academy-id "q-76376" :question/problem "Find the first term of an arithmetic series if its $17$th term is $33$ and the sum of the first $30$ terms is $1\\,080.$" :question/worked-solution "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=30$ and ${S}_{N}=1\\,080$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 1\\,080 & =\\frac{30}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(30-1)d) \\\\ 1\\,080 & =15(2{a}_{1}+29d) \\\\ \\frac{1\\,080}{15} & =2{a}_{1}+29d \\\\ 72 & =2{a}_{1}+29d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $17$th term of the arithmetic series  and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{17} & ={a}_{1}+(17-1)d \\\\ 33 & ={a}_{1}+16d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}33={a}_{1}+16d \\\\ 72=2{a}_{1}+29d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-66 & =-2{a}_{1}-32d \\\\ 72 & =2{a}_{1}+29d \\\\ 6 & =-3d \\\\ d & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d=-2$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}33 & ={a}_{1}+16(-2) \\\\ 33 & ={a}_{1}-32 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =65.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-76376/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07a3dfec-3f7b-5820-9be5-12bf4acd5a3b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76376"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-108635/selection/9b32bd1c2d85515eb67bf6ed1aa42ff7a66b88544eaafce7b11ad994fbde1d11" :answer/id #uuid "ddb65509-f820-5cc1-b9a2-8034ce4c3a19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108635/selection/1953fffdd5464c00598a8fc81fdbe9a25a6903f89c460eaf7b2d56ffaf15695e" :answer/id #uuid "685a628d-443f-50ef-b9f2-c8d7b74a8c72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108635/selection/09a797f0254edd22776128e046edd3557657fb445dcc367842699960b6d091f0" :answer/id #uuid "4b44b3d1-7455-5f33-98cd-4fd61f0fdf53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108635/selection/9db8bb3a8fca0a53f1a66296f215433b5fba29bca2325a9035c810088be55a44" :answer/id #uuid "fc9ff94a-d9cc-57b1-80fc-2cd1efd653ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108635/selection/336de2bb8f0e1e5bec5444214921ab4007f840558e694e1651575347e5aed4f7" :answer/id #uuid "7f2e66ae-72ef-51bc-add8-20990f38fa3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108635/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6cc8317b-b558-516f-89b7-3e78ee5e6762" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-108635/selection/336de2bb8f0e1e5bec5444214921ab4007f840558e694e1651575347e5aed4f7" :answer-field/choices ["q-108635/selection/9b32bd1c2d85515eb67bf6ed1aa42ff7a66b88544eaafce7b11ad994fbde1d11" "q-108635/selection/1953fffdd5464c00598a8fc81fdbe9a25a6903f89c460eaf7b2d56ffaf15695e" "q-108635/selection/09a797f0254edd22776128e046edd3557657fb445dcc367842699960b6d091f0" "q-108635/selection/9db8bb3a8fca0a53f1a66296f215433b5fba29bca2325a9035c810088be55a44" "q-108635/selection/336de2bb8f0e1e5bec5444214921ab4007f840558e694e1651575347e5aed4f7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-108635" :question/id #uuid "f48376ce-40f3-53df-8262-cf6ddaed1567" :question/math-academy-id "q-108635" :question/problem "What is the first term of an arithmetic series if the common difference is $d=0.6,$ and the sum of the first $37$ terms is ${S}_{37}=444?$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the common difference of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=37$, $d=0.6$, and ${S}_{N}=444$ into the formula above, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}444 & =\\frac{37}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(37-1)(0.6)) \\\\ 888 & =37(2{a}_{1}+21.6) \\\\ \\frac{888}{37} & =2{a}_{1}+21.6 \\\\ 2.4 & =2{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =1.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-108635/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f9251ee-4d19-5074-a2a3-07e13149260f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-108635"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-108637/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "ce0fdce3-8392-5967-9f81-f041a1c3c674" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108637/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer/id #uuid "d10f67f3-e3a5-59b2-ac48-761a46619e20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108637/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "924c4bce-ef7a-5f25-8774-6a91e18d2288" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108637/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "442ad632-b186-59d7-b03e-13516bdf5927" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108637/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "18ccd489-19d4-5c15-8bfc-e40de8e0f34f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108637/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b24a8251-4adc-524e-a1bc-b29c7a641046" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-108637/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-108637/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-108637/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" "q-108637/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-108637/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-108637/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-108637" :question/id #uuid "5fe6fe0a-1ed0-5284-b975-bb2f6d1174c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-108637" :question/problem "What is the first term of an arithmetic series if the common difference is $d=\\frac{5}{7},$ and the sum of the first $50$ terms is ${S}_{50}=1\\,125?$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the common difference of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=50$, $d=\\frac{5}{7}$, and ${S}_{N}=1\\,125$ into the formula above, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1\\,125 & =\\frac{50}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(50-1)(\\frac{5}{7})) \\\\ 1\\,125 & =25(2{a}_{1}+35) \\\\ 45 & =2{a}_{1}+35 \\\\ 10 & =2{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-108637/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f9251ee-4d19-5074-a2a3-07e13149260f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-108637"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-250865/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "b8292cad-17b0-54fa-9fb3-b8b754f481b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-250865/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9153e017-e2b8-5cb0-b46d-fb67ba33257f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-250865/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-250865/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-250865" :question/id #uuid "3e9bdeaa-b79d-5303-b727-c7dd990da898" :question/math-academy-id "q-250865" :question/problem "If the $10$th term of an arithmetic series is $-\\frac{1}{5}$ and the sum of the first $21$ terms is $0,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=21$ and ${S}_{N}=0$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{21}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(21-1)d) \\\\ 0 & =21(2{a}_{1}+20d) \\\\ 0 & =2{a}_{1}+20d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $10$th term of the arithmetic series and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{10} & ={a}_{1}+(10-1)d \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5} & ={a}_{1}+9d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{5} & \\,\\,\\,=\\,{a}_{1}+9d \\\\ \\,0 & \\,\\,\\,=\\,2{a}_{1}+20d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5} & =-2{a}_{1}-18d \\\\ 0 & =2{a}_{1}+20d \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & =2d \\\\ d & =\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d=\\frac{1}{5}$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{5} & ={a}_{1}+9d \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5} & ={a}_{1}+9(\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5} & ={a}_{1}+\\frac{9}{5} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-250865/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07a3dfec-3f7b-5820-9be5-12bf4acd5a3b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-250865"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
